---
name: relationship_memory
description: >
  One seeded relationship, as a t=0 observation memory in an agent's stream
  (backend/seed.py, relationship_statements -> seed_relationships; issue #779).
  Built from a world YAML's validated `relationships` edge -- authored once under
  its first-named persona, seeded into BOTH ends' memory, each from its own side.
  The other person is named in full deliberately: the conversation path retrieves
  with `query=listener.name` (text_adventure_games/conversation.py), so naming
  them is what makes the prior surface in the dialogue that needs it. Memory
  text, not a live model prompt.
inputs:
  other:
    type: string
    description: The person on the other end of the edge, e.g. "Bethany Cole".
  kind:
    type: string
    description: >
      The relationship label, verbatim from the edge, e.g. "rivals" /
      "reporter & source" / "TA & student". Optional -- omitted when the edge
      left it blank, leaving just "I know <other>."
  closeness_note:
    type: string
    description: >
      The edge's 1..5 closeness as a sentence (see seed.CLOSENESS_PHRASE), e.g.
      "We know each other a little." Optional; empty contributes nothing.
  description:
    type: string
    description: >
      The edge's authored natural-language description, appended verbatim -- it
      is the author's own framing of the relationship, so it is never rewritten.
      Optional.
sample:
  other: Bethany Cole
  kind: rivals
  closeness_note: We know each other a little.
  description: Omar and Bethany are the two front-runners for student body
    president -- civil in public, fiercely competitive about every endorsement.
---
I know {{ other }}{% if kind %}: {{ kind }}{% endif %}.{% if closeness_note %} {{ closeness_note }}{% endif %}{% if description %} {{ description }}{% endif %}
